-- ccc23-reviews.l4 -- sections 672.81 to 672.852 (Review of Dispositions; Power to Compel Appearance; Stay of Proceedings) of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46; 672.83(2) is repealed.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively), from the text alone. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation
-- (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Form: see the header of ccc23-assessment.l4. The months and years of this section are calendar periods: dates are `Date day month year` and `add months` rolls the month and clamps the day of the month.

§ `Section 672.81 -- Mandatory review of dispositions`

-- 672.81(1.3): for the purposes of subsection (1.2), serious personal injury offence means (a) an indictable offence involving any of the following in respect of another person, including the accused's intimate partner, a member of the intimate partner's family and a member of the accused's family:
-- (i) the use or attempted use of violence against the other person, or (ii) conduct endangering or likely to endanger the life or safety of -- or conduct inflicting or likely to inflict severe psychological damage on -- the other person; or (b) an indictable offence referred to in section 151, 152, 153, 153.1, 155, 160, 170, 171, 172, 271, 272 or 273 or an attempt to commit such an offence.
-- The sections of paragraph (b) are tested against the core record `Provision of the Code` (rule R1 of PLAN.md). The text defines the term "for the purposes of subsection (1.2)"; section 672.64(1) and 672.84 use it by reference to this subsection.
-- fork: F-SUCH-OFFENCE
-- src:13920 | (1.3) For the purposes of subsection (1.2), serious personal injury offence means
-- src:13921 | (a) an indictable offence involving any of the following in respect of another person, including the accused’s intimate partner, a member of the intimate partner’s family and a member of the accused’s family:
-- src:13922 | (i) the use or attempted use of violence against the other person, or
-- src:13923 | (ii) conduct endangering or likely to endanger the life or safety of — or conduct inflicting or likely to inflict severe psychological damage on — the other person; or
-- src:13924 | (b) an indictable offence referred to in section 151, 152, 153, 153.1, 155, 160, 170, 171, 172, 271, 272 or 273 or an attempt to commit such an offence.
@ref s 672.81(1.3); s 672.81(1.3)"serious personal injury offence"; s 672.81(1.3)(a); s 672.81(1.3)(a)(i); s 672.81(1.3)(a)(ii); s 672.81(1.3)(b) (src:13920-13924)
GIVEN offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `it is an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an attempt to commit the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it involves, in respect of another person, the use or attempted use of violence against the other person` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)(i)
      `it involves, in respect of another person, conduct endangering or likely to endanger the life or safety of, or conduct inflicting or likely to inflict severe psychological damage on, the other person` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)(ii)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.81(1.3) serious personal injury offence` MEANS
    IF `limb (a): an indictable offence involving violence or endangering conduct` OR `limb (b): an indictable offence referred to in a listed section, or an attempt`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "serious personal injury offence means"
    WHERE
        `limb (a): an indictable offence involving violence or endangering conduct` MEANS
            `it is an indictable offence` AND (`it involves, in respect of another person, the use or attempted use of violence against the other person` OR `it involves, in respect of another person, conduct endangering or likely to endanger the life or safety of, or conduct inflicting or likely to inflict severe psychological damage on, the other person`)
        `limb (b): an indictable offence referred to in a listed section, or an attempt` MEANS
            elem (offence's `section`) (LIST 151, 152, 153, 153.1, 155, 160, 170, 171, 172, 271, 272, 273) AND (`it is an indictable offence` OR `it is an attempt to commit the offence`)

-- 672.81(1): a Review Board shall hold a hearing not later than twelve months after making a disposition and every twelve months thereafter for as long as the disposition remains in force, to review any disposition that it has made in respect of an accused, other than an absolute discharge under paragraph 672.54(a).
-- As a regulative rule: the Review Board's duty, within the days to the day twelve months after the disposition (or after the last review).
-- src:13911 | 672.81 (1) A Review Board shall hold a hearing not later than twelve months after making a disposition and every twelve months thereafter for as long as the disposition remains in force, to review any disposition that it has made in respect of an accused, other than an absolute discharge under paragraph 672.54(a).
@ref s 672.81(1) (src:13911)
DECLARE `s 672.81(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 672.81(1) hold a hearing to review the disposition`

@ref s 672.81(1) (src:13911)
GIVEN `the day the disposition was made or last reviewed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 672.81(1) act`
`s 672.81(1) the Review Board must hold a hearing within twelve months` MEANS
    PARTY `a Review Board`
    MUST `s 672.81(1) hold a hearing to review the disposition`
    WITHIN (Day (`add months` `the day the disposition was made or last reviewed` 12) MINUS Day `the day the disposition was made or last reviewed`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a Review Board` BECAUSE "no hearing was held within twelve months after the disposition was made or last reviewed"

-- 672.81(1.1): despite (1), the Review Board may extend the time for holding a hearing to a maximum of twenty-four months after the making or reviewing of a disposition if the accused is represented by counsel and the accused and the Attorney General consent to the extension.
-- fork: F-GRANT-IF, F-CAP
-- src:13913 | (1.1) Despite subsection (1), the Review Board may extend the time for holding a hearing to a maximum of twenty-four months after the making or reviewing of a disposition if the accused is represented by counsel and the accused and the Attorney General consent to the extension.
@ref s 672.81(1.1) (src:13913)
GIVEN `the accused is represented by counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused consents to the extension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General consents to the extension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the months after the making or reviewing of the disposition to which the time is extended` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.81(1.1) the Review Board may extend the time for holding the hearing to a maximum of twenty-four months` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the months after the making or reviewing of the disposition to which the time is extended` GREATER THAN 24 THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to a maximum of twenty-four months after the making or reviewing of a disposition"
        IF `the accused is represented by counsel` AND `the accused consents to the extension` AND `the Attorney General consents to the extension` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the accused is represented by counsel and the accused and the Attorney General consent to the extension"

-- 672.81(1.2): despite (1), at the conclusion of a hearing under this section the Review Board may, after making a disposition, extend the time for holding a subsequent hearing under this section to a maximum of twenty-four months if (a) the accused has been found not criminally responsible for a serious personal injury offence;
-- (b) the accused is subject to a disposition made under paragraph 672.54(c); and (c) the Review Board is satisfied on the basis of any relevant information, including disposition information within the meaning of subsection 672.51(1) and an assessment report made under an assessment ordered under paragraph 672.121(a),
-- that the condition of the accused is not likely to improve and that detention remains necessary for the period of the extension.
-- fork: F-GRANT-IF, F-CAP
-- src:13915 | (1.2) Despite subsection (1), at the conclusion of a hearing under this section the Review Board may, after making a disposition, extend the time for holding a subsequent hearing under this section to a maximum of twenty-four months if
-- src:13916 | (a) the accused has been found not crimi­nally responsible for a serious personal injury offence;
-- src:13917 | (b) the accused is subject to a disposition made under paragraph 672.54(c); and
-- src:13918 | (c) the Review Board is satisfied on the basis of any relevant information, including disposition information within the meaning of subsection 672.51(1) and an assessment report made under an assessment ordered under paragraph 672.121(a), that the condition of the accused is not likely to improve and that detention remains necessary for the period of the extension.
@ref s 672.81(1.2); s 672.81(1.2)(a); s 672.81(1.2)(b); s 672.81(1.2)(c) (src:13915-13918)
GIVEN `it is at the conclusion of a hearing under section 672.81, after making a disposition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused has been found not criminally responsible for a serious personal injury offence, by s 672.81(1.3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `the accused is subject to a disposition made under paragraph 672.54(c)` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
      `the Review Board is satisfied that the condition of the accused is not likely to improve and that detention remains necessary for the period of the extension` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
      `the months to which the time is extended` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.81(1.2) the Review Board may extend the time for holding a subsequent hearing to a maximum of twenty-four months` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the months to which the time is extended` GREATER THAN 24 THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to a maximum of twenty-four months"
        IF `it is at the conclusion of a hearing under section 672.81, after making a disposition` AND `the accused has been found not criminally responsible for a serious personal injury offence, by s 672.81(1.3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the accused is subject to a disposition made under paragraph 672.54(c)` AND `the Review Board is satisfied that the condition of the accused is not likely to improve and that detention remains necessary for the period of the extension` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if (a) the accused has been found not criminally responsible for a serious personal injury offence; (b) the accused is subject to a disposition made under paragraph 672.54(c); and (c) the Review Board is satisfied"

-- 672.81(1.31): despite subsections (1) to (1.2), the Review Board may extend the time for holding a hearing in respect of a high-risk accused to a maximum of 36 months after making or reviewing a disposition if the accused is represented by counsel and the accused and the Attorney General consent to the extension.
-- fork: F-GRANT-IF, F-CAP
-- src:13926 | (1.31) Despite subsections (1) to (1.2), the Review Board may extend the time for holding a hearing in respect of a high-risk accused to a maximum of 36 months after making or reviewing a disposition if the accused is represented by counsel and the accused and the Attorney General consent to the extension.
