        IF `the accused is represented by counsel` AND `the accused consents to the extension` AND `the Attorney General consents to the extension` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the accused is represented by counsel and the accused and the Attorney General consent to the extension"

-- 672.81(1.32): despite subsections (1) to (1.2), at the conclusion of a hearing under subsection 672.47(4) or this section in respect of a high-risk accused, the Review Board may, after making a disposition, extend the time for holding a subsequent hearing under this section to a maximum of 36 months
-- if the Review Board is satisfied on the basis of any relevant information, including disposition information as defined in subsection 672.51(1) and an assessment report made under an assessment ordered under paragraph 672.121(c), that the accused's condition is not likely to improve and that detention remains necessary for the period of the extension.
-- fork: F-GRANT-IF, F-CAP
-- src:13928 | (1.32) Despite subsections (1) to (1.2), at the conclusion of a hearing under subsection 672.47(4) or this section in respect of a high-risk accused, the Review Board may, after making a disposition, extend the time for holding a subsequent hearing under this section to a maximum of 36 months if the Review Board is satisfied on the basis of any relevant information, including disposition information as defined in subsection 672.51(1) and an assessment report made under an assessment ordered under paragraph 672.121(c), that the accused’s condition is not likely to improve and that detention remains necessary for the period of the extension.
@ref s 672.81(1.32) (src:13928)
GIVEN `the accused is a high-risk accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is at the conclusion of a hearing under subsection 672.47(4) or section 672.81, after making a disposition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Review Board is satisfied that the accused’s condition is not likely to improve and that detention remains necessary for the period of the extension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the months to which the time is extended` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.81(1.32) the Review Board may extend the time for holding a subsequent hearing in respect of a high-risk accused to a maximum of 36 months` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the accused is a high-risk accused` AND `it is at the conclusion of a hearing under subsection 672.47(4) or section 672.81, after making a disposition`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at the conclusion of a hearing under subsection 672.47(4) or this section in respect of a high-risk accused"
        IF `the months to which the time is extended` GREATER THAN 36 THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to a maximum of 36 months"
        IF `the Review Board is satisfied that the accused’s condition is not likely to improve and that detention remains necessary for the period of the extension` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the Review Board is satisfied on the basis of any relevant information"

-- The longest time before the next hearing, in months, with the extensions of (1.1), (1.2), (1.31) and (1.32): each extension answer is an input (JUST TRUE = the extension is open). The text's order of generosity: 36, 24, 12.
-- src:13911 | 672.81 (1) A Review Board shall hold a hearing not later than twelve months after making a disposition and every twelve months thereafter for as long as the disposition remains in force, to review any disposition that it has made in respect of an accused, other than an absolute discharge under paragraph 672.54(a).
