-- src:13919 | Definition of serious personal injury offence
-- src:13920 | (1.3) For the purposes of subsection (1.2), serious personal injury offence means
-- src:13921 | (a) an indictable offence involving any of the following in respect of another person, including the accused’s intimate partner, a member of the intimate partner’s family and a member of the accused’s family:
-- src:13922 | (i) the use or attempted use of violence against the other person, or
-- src:13923 | (ii) conduct endangering or likely to endanger the life or safety of — or conduct inflicting or likely to inflict severe psychological damage on — the other person; or
-- src:13924 | (b) an indictable offence referred to in section 151, 152, 153, 153.1, 155, 160, 170, 171, 172, 271, 272 or 273 or an attempt to commit such an offence.
-- src:13925 | Extension on consent — high-risk accused
-- src:13926 | (1.31) Despite subsections (1) to (1.2), the Review Board may extend the time for holding a hearing in respect of a high-risk accused to a maximum of 36 months after making or reviewing a disposition if the accused is represented by counsel and the accused and the Attorney General consent to the extension.
-- src:13927 | Extension — no likely improvement
-- src:13928 | (1.32) Despite subsections (1) to (1.2), at the conclusion of a hearing under subsection 672.47(4) or this section in respect of a high-risk accused, the Review Board may, after making a disposition, extend the time for holding a subsequent hearing under this section to a maximum of 36 months if the Review Board is satisfied on the basis of any relevant information, including disposition information as defined in subsection 672.51(1) and an assessment report made under an assessment ordered under paragraph 672.121(c), that the accused’s condition is not likely to improve and that detention remains necessary for the period of the extension.
@ref s 672.81(1); s 672.81(1.1); s 672.81(1.2); s 672.81(1.31); s 672.81(1.32) (src:13911-13928)
GIVEN `the extension to 24 months by consent is open, by s 672.81(1.1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the extension to 24 months for a serious personal injury offence is open, by s 672.81(1.2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the extension to 36 months by consent for a high-risk accused is open, by s 672.81(1.31)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the extension to 36 months for a high-risk accused whose condition is not likely to improve is open, by s 672.81(1.32)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 672.81 the longest time before the next hearing, in months` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the extension to 36 months by consent for a high-risk accused is open, by s 672.81(1.31)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the extension to 36 months for a high-risk accused whose condition is not likely to improve is open, by s 672.81(1.32)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN 36
        IF `the extension to 24 months by consent is open, by s 672.81(1.1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the extension to 24 months for a serious personal injury offence is open, by s 672.81(1.2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN 24
        OTHERWISE 12

-- The duty of (1) as a decision function over dates, with the months allowed (12, or the extended maximum): the hearing is held not later than that many months after the disposition was made or last reviewed.
-- fork: F-MUST-BARE
-- src:13911 | 672.81 (1) A Review Board shall hold a hearing not later than twelve months after making a disposition and every twelve months thereafter for as long as the disposition remains in force, to review any disposition that it has made in respect of an accused, other than an absolute discharge under paragraph 672.54(a).
@ref s 672.81(1) (src:13911)
GIVEN `the Review Board is reviewing a disposition other than an absolute discharge under paragraph 672.54(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the disposition was made or last reviewed` IS A DATE
      `the day the Review Board holds the hearing` IS A DATE
      `the months allowed, by s 672.81 the longest time before the next hearing, in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.81(1) the Review Board has held the hearing in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Review Board is reviewing a disposition other than an absolute discharge under paragraph 672.54(a)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "other than an absolute discharge under paragraph 672.54(a)"
        IF `the day the Review Board holds the hearing` AT MOST (`add months` `the day the disposition was made or last reviewed` `the months allowed, by s 672.81 the longest time before the next hearing, in months`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not later than twelve months after making a disposition and every twelve months thereafter"

-- 672.81(1.4): if the Review Board extends the time for holding a hearing under subsection (1.2) or (1.32), it shall provide notice of the extension to the accused, the prosecutor and the person in charge of the hospital where the accused is detained.
