-- 672.81(3): where an accused is detained in custody pursuant to a disposition made under paragraph 672.54(c) and a sentence of imprisonment is subsequently imposed on the accused in respect of another offence, the Review Board shall hold a hearing to review the disposition as soon as is practicable after receiving notice of that sentence.
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
-- src:13938 | (3) Where an accused is detained in custody pursuant to a disposition made under paragraph 672.54(c) and a sentence of imprisonment is subsequently imposed on the accused in respect of another offence, the Review Board shall hold a hearing to review the disposition as soon as is practicable after receiving notice of that sentence.
@ref s 672.81(3) (src:13938)
GIVEN `the accused is detained in custody pursuant to a disposition made under paragraph 672.54(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a sentence of imprisonment is subsequently imposed on the accused in respect of another offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Review Board receives notice of that sentence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.81(3) the Review Board must hold a hearing to review the disposition as soon as is practicable` MEANS
    IF `the accused is detained in custody pursuant to a disposition made under paragraph 672.54(c)` AND `a sentence of imprisonment is subsequently imposed on the accused in respect of another offence` AND `the Review Board receives notice of that sentence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused is detained in custody pursuant to a disposition made under paragraph 672.54(c) and a sentence of imprisonment is subsequently imposed on the accused in respect of another offence"

§ `Sections 672.82 and 672.83 -- Discretionary review; disposition by Review Board`

-- 672.82(1): a Review Board may hold a hearing to review any of its dispositions at any time, of its own motion or at the request of the accused or any other party.
-- src:13940 | 672.82 (1) A Review Board may hold a hearing to review any of its dispositions at any time, of its own motion or at the request of the accused or any other party.
@ref s 672.82(1) (src:13940)
GIVEN `it is a disposition of the Review Board` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.82(1) the Review Board may hold a hearing to review any of its dispositions at any time` MEANS
    IF `it is a disposition of the Review Board`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to review any of its dispositions"

-- 672.82(1.1): where a Review Board holds a hearing under subsection (1) of its own motion, it shall provide notice to the prosecutor, the accused and any other party.
