    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court is determining whether a stay of proceedings is in the interests of the proper administration of justice` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In order to determine whether a stay of proceedings is in the interests of the proper administration of justice"
        IF `it is a submission of the prosecutor, the accused or any other party` OR `it is the nature and seriousness of the alleged offence` OR `it is the salutary and deleterious effects of the order for a stay of proceedings, including any effect on public confidence in the administration of justice` OR `it is the time that has elapsed since the commission of the alleged offence and whether an inquiry has been held under section 672.33` OR `it is any other factor that the court considers relevant` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a factor that the court does not consider relevant is not named

-- 672.851(9): if a stay of proceedings is ordered by the court, any disposition made in respect of the accused ceases to have effect. If a stay of proceedings is not ordered, the finding of unfit to stand trial and any disposition made in respect of the accused remain in force,
-- until the Review Board holds a disposition hearing and makes a disposition in respect of the accused under section 672.83.
-- src:13998 | (9) If a stay of proceedings is ordered by the court, any disposition made in respect of the accused ceases to have effect. If a stay of proceedings is not ordered, the finding of unfit to stand trial and any disposition made in respect of the accused remain in force, until the Review Board holds a disposition hearing and makes a disposition in respect of the accused under section 672.83.
@ref s 672.851(9) (src:13998)
DECLARE `s 672.851(9) effect` IS ONE OF
    `s 672.851(9) any disposition made in respect of the accused ceases to have effect`
    `s 672.851(9) the finding of unfit to stand trial and any disposition made in respect of the accused remain in force`
    `s 672.851(9) not covered`

@ref s 672.851(9) (src:13998)
GIVEN `the inquiry is complete` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a stay of proceedings is ordered by the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Review Board has held a disposition hearing and made a disposition under section 672.83` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 672.851(9) effect`
`s 672.851(9) the effect of the court’s decision on a stay of proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the inquiry is complete` THEN `s 672.851(9) not covered`   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of the outcome of the court's inquiry
        IF `a stay of proceedings is ordered by the court` THEN `s 672.851(9) any disposition made in respect of the accused ceases to have effect`
        IF `the Review Board has held a disposition hearing and made a disposition under section 672.83` THEN `s 672.851(9) not covered`   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "until the Review Board holds a disposition hearing and makes a disposition in respect of the accused under section 672.83"
        OTHERWISE `s 672.851(9) the finding of unfit to stand trial and any disposition made in respect of the accused remain in force`

-- 672.852(1): the Court of Appeal may allow an appeal against an order made under subsection 672.851(7) for a stay of proceedings, if the Court of Appeal is of the opinion that the order is unreasonable or cannot be supported by the evidence.
-- fork: F-GRANT-IF
-- src:14000 | 672.852 (1) The Court of Appeal may allow an appeal against an order made under subsection 672.851(7) for a stay of proceedings, if the Court of Appeal is of the opinion that the order is unreasonable or cannot be supported by the evidence.
@ref s 672.852(1) (src:14000)
GIVEN `the Court of Appeal is of the opinion that the order is unreasonable or cannot be supported by the evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.852(1) the Court of Appeal may allow an appeal against the order for a stay of proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the Court of Appeal is of the opinion that the order is unreasonable or cannot be supported by the evidence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the Court of Appeal is of the opinion that the order is unreasonable or cannot be supported by the evidence"

-- 672.852(2): if the Court of Appeal allows the appeal, it may set aside the order for a stay of proceedings and restore the finding that the accused is unfit to stand trial and the disposition made in respect of the accused.
-- fork: F-GRANT-IF
